When the townspeople had worshiped the goddess, she said to them that your prayer is accepted.
I am pleased.
Then, fulfilling his goal, Lord Krishna appeared before them with his new wife,
and filled them with joy. The available Hrishikesha has returned again. Along with wives, jewels, and all kinds of festivals. 7. Meaning of the word

Available—to be recognized; Hrishikesham—to the lord of the senses; Mrutam—a dead person; Punah—again; Iva—as if; Aagatam—arrived; Saha—with; Pattanya—of the wife; Mani—a gem; Greevam—in the neck; Sarve—all; Jata—born; Maha—very;
Utsavah—laughter and joy. Seeing Lord Hrishikesh with his new wife and the Syamantaka jewel around his neck, all the people were overjoyed, as if Krishna had returned from death. Meaning: According to Srila Vishwanath Chakravarti, when Jambavan presented his daughter Krishna,
he put that gem around her neck. Satrajit, having been welcomed in the assembly, in the presence of the king.
