And having developed the intellect, may you be victorious, son of Satrajit. Manim cha swayamudyamya krishnayopajahar ha. 4. Meaning of the word

Evam—in this way; Vivasitah—with firm resolve; Buddhaya—with the use of intellect; Satrajit—Satrajit; Swa—own;
Sutam—daughter; Shubham—of fair complexion; Manim—gem; Cha—and; Swayam—self; Udyamya—by making an effort; Krishnaya—to Krishna; Upajahar ha—gave. In this way, with wisdom, strengthening the mind, King Satrajit himself, along with his fair-complexioned daughter, arranged to offer Syamantaka jewel to Lord Krishna. Ta Satyabhamaam Bhagavanupayem yathavidhi. Of many virtues, of a virtuous form, endowed with qualities of excellence. 44. Meaning of the word

Tam—That; Satyabhamaam—From Satyabhama; Bhagavan—By God; Upayame—By marriage; Yatha-vidhi—By proper rituals;
Bahubhih—By many people; Yachitam—Asked for; Sheel—Of excellent character; Roop—Beauty; Audarya—And generosity; Guna—Of virtues;
Anvitam—United, complete.
The Lord married Satyabhama in due religious rites. Because of being endowed with excellent conduct,
beauty, generosity, and other virtues, many people wanted to take him.
Was. Meaning: Srila Sridhar Swami says that people like Kritavarma wanted to marry Satyabhama. O King, I do not wish for any jewel. We are the fruit-bearers of the devotees of the Lord. 45. Meaning of the word

